*   The problem is a neighborhood search in 2D.
    *   Points are sorted by their x-coordinate.
    *   For each point `i`, the code searches for neighbors within a distance `r`.
    *   It optimizes the search by only checking points `j` where `|x[j] - x[i]| <= r`.
    *   The workload is irregular: some points are in dense clusters, requiring more distance checks than others.
    *   Target machine: Apple M4 (4 P-cores, 6 E-cores).
    *   OpenMP 5.1 is available.
    *   Constraints: Only modify the `kernel` function.

    ```c
    static void kernel(long n, double r, const double *x, const double *y, int *nb) {
        for (long i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int c = 0;
            for (long j = i + 1; j < n && x[j] - x[i] <= r; j++) {
                double dx = x[j] - x[i], dy = y[j] - y[i];
                if (dx * dx + dy * dy <= r * r) c++;
            }
            for (long j = i - 1; j >= 0 && x[i] - x[j] <= r; j--) {
                double dx = x[i] - x[j], dy = y[i] - y[j];
                if (dx * dx + dy * dy <= r * r) c++;
            }
            nb[i] = c;
        }
    }
    ```

